     override)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Merge a dictionary of override values for self\&.connection_pool_kw\&.

This does not modify self\&.connection_pool_kw and returns a new dict\&.
Any keys in the override dictionary with a value of ``None`` are
removed from the merged dictionary\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " \fBHTTPConnectionPool\fP urllib3\&.poolmanager\&.PoolManager\&._new_pool ( self, str scheme, str host, int port, dict[str, typing\&.Any] | None  request_context = \fCNone\fP)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Create a new :class:`urllib3\&.connectionpool\&.ConnectionPool` based on host, port, scheme, and
any additional pool keyword arguments\&.

If ``request_context`` is provided, it is provided as keyword arguments
to the pool class used\&. This method is used to actually create the
connection pools handed out by :meth:`connection_from_url` and
companion methods\&. It is intended to be overridden for customization\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " bool urllib3\&.poolmanager\&.PoolManager\&._proxy_requires_url_absolute_form ( self, \fBUrl\fP parsed_url)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Indicates if the proxy requires the complete destination URL in the
request\&.  Normally this is only needed when not using an HTTP CONNECT
tunnel\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " None urllib3\&.poolmanager\&.PoolManager\&.clear ( self)"

.PP
.nf
Empty our store of pools and direct them all to close\&.

This will not affect in-flight connections, but they will not be
re-used after completion\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " \fBHTTPConnectionPool\fP urllib3\&.poolmanager\&.PoolManager\&.connection_from_context ( self, dict[str, typing\&.Any]
     request_context)"

.PP
.nf
Get a :class:`urllib3\&.connectionpool\&.ConnectionPool` based on the request context\&.

``request_context`` must at least contain the ``scheme`` key and its
value must be a key in ``key_fn_by_scheme`` instance variable\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " \fBHTTPConnectionPool\fP urllib3\&.poolmanager\&.PoolManager\&.connection_from_host ( self, str | None host, int | None  port = \fCNone\fP, str | None  scheme = \fC'http'\fP, dict[str, typing\&.Any] | None  pool_kwargs = \fCNone\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Get a :class:`urllib3\&.connectionpool\&.ConnectionPool` based on the host, port, and scheme\&.

If ``port`` isn't given, it will be derived from the ``scheme`` using
``urllib3\&.connectionpool\&.port_by_scheme``\&. If ``pool_kwargs`` is
provided, it is merged with the instance's ``connection_pool_kw``
variable and used to create the new connection pool, if one is
needed\&.

.fi
.PP
 
