.SS " \fBHTTPConnectionPool\fP urllib3\&.poolmanager\&.PoolManager\&.connection_from_pool_key ( self, \fBPoolKey\fP pool_key, dict[str, typing\&.Any]
     request_context)"

.PP
.nf
Get a :class:`urllib3\&.connectionpool\&.ConnectionPool` based on the provided pool key\&.

``pool_key`` should be a namedtuple that only contains immutable
objects\&. At a minimum it must have the ``scheme``, ``host``, and
``port`` fields\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " \fBHTTPConnectionPool\fP urllib3\&.poolmanager\&.PoolManager\&.connection_from_url ( self, str url, dict[str, typing\&.Any] | None  pool_kwargs = \fCNone\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Similar to :func:`urllib3\&.connectionpool\&.connection_from_url`\&.

If ``pool_kwargs`` is not provided and a new pool needs to be
constructed, ``self\&.connection_pool_kw`` is used to initialize
the :class:`urllib3\&.connectionpool\&.ConnectionPool`\&. If ``pool_kwargs``
is provided, it is used instead\&. Note that if a new pool does not
need to be created for the request, the provided ``pool_kwargs`` are
not used\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " \fBBaseHTTPResponse\fP urllib3\&.poolmanager\&.PoolManager\&.urlopen ( self, str method, str url, bool  redirect = \fCTrue\fP, **typing\&.Any
     kw)"

.PP
.nf
Same as :meth:`urllib3\&.HTTPConnectionPool\&.urlopen`
with custom cross-host redirect logic and only sends the request-uri
portion of the ``url``\&.

The given ``url`` parameter must be absolute, such that an appropriate
:class:`urllib3\&.connectionpool\&.ConnectionPool` can be chosen for it\&.

.fi
.PP
 
